A||||4||Tweek||Outside mirror removal and manuel window crank||||1||
Z||000000||Tweek||05-16-2001||03:13 PM||||Im in the process of removing a few thing from my now smahed up drivers door. Ive got the inside panel ready to take off, but I cant figure out how to remove the window crank...  is it absolutly necessary to have the special tool for this??<P><BR>Also, more importantly I have the mirror assembly unbolted, but the cable are still attached to the little controller, and the hole I need to pull then through is only about 3/4 of an in.<BR>Upon doing a search I didnt see where anyone else had encountered this problem, and it wasnt specifically mentioned in the cave, although many thanks to the Ogre for all of the other info I have used from there!<P>Ciao||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tweek||05-16-2001||03:41 PM||||NM..  I figured out the mirror, for archive purposes there is a little allen bolt, that loosens the controller so that assembly can be removed.<P>I think I'm just gonna go to the store to see if I can find that tool for the window crank.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||05-16-2001||03:46 PM||||Tweek,<BR>That tool isn't terribly expensive, and the little clip on the window crank is a PITA without it.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||05-16-2001||04:41 PM||||its a flat piece of metal with a funny shaped notch cut in it. prob only $4or$5 just slide it in from the handle side till it stops then pull it back out, handle should just fall off. watch for the little wire 'C' shaped clip. If it dont try it from 180*, they can be put on backwards. to put handle back on, slip the clip back in groves and just push handle back on till it catches.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierohoho||05-16-2001||07:18 PM||||Tweek, In the past I just make a little "J" hook out of a piece of wire and fish that onto the end or middle of the "C" shaped clip and pull. The "J" should be about the size of the letter j on a printed page. When you get it out the handle slides off. Easy to make with a needle nose pliers and free.||||reg||1
